 PM MDT Sunday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding along the Rio Grande and low lying agricultural\nareas in Rio Grande and Alamosa counties is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 525 PM MDT, Emergency management reports flooding of low lying\nareas along and near the Rio Grande in Rio Grande county and in\nAlamosa county upstream of the city of Alamosa.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties between Monte Vista and Alamosa.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-25T21:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dec66dcc50c62eb3136a29e188c17eb9595591f1.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dec66dcc50c62eb3136a29e188c17eb9595591f1.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-25T23:29:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 252329 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 529 PM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Another 18 hours of showers, then we dry out. - Mainly dry this upcoming week, then another potentially active event for later next weekend. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH MONDAY NIGHT/... Issued at 115 PM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026 With the mid level trough still to our west, ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-25T06:59:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 250659 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1259 AM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-260700- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":